WEBVTT

00:01.303 --> 00:03.756
That's a great looking set of knives.
Where'd you get those?

00:03.826 --> 00:06.056
Well, this old magician guy
was trying to unload 'em.

00:06.106 --> 00:09.121
- Like, magical trick knives or...?
- Well, the knives are real.

00:09.171 --> 00:11.540
I mean, they're used for magical
tricks, but they're real.

00:11.606 --> 00:13.399
They're sharp, too.
Well, I'll show you.

00:13.475 --> 00:15.841
Dee, can you get up against
the wall for a second?

00:15.878 --> 00:17.470
No. You're not throwing knives at me.

00:17.732 --> 00:19.139
Let's throw them, regardless.

00:19.196 --> 00:20.932
Start running, 'cause we're coming.

00:21.194 --> 00:22.906
- Ten, nine,
- Don't you dare.

00:22.981 --> 00:24.628
eight, seven,

00:24.704 --> 00:27.647
- six, five, four...
- Okay, listen up, everybody!

00:27.909 --> 00:30.274
- We're in the middle of something.
- I got news.

00:30.536 --> 00:31.913
Your mother is dead. Ha!

00:33.748 --> 00:36.613
- Nice try. Very funny, Frank.
- I'm serious, this time.

00:36.876 --> 00:38.602
She had a botched neck lift.

00:38.904 --> 00:40.701
She's as dead as disco.

00:42.465 --> 00:44.072
Who wants champagne?

00:44.717 --> 00:47.349
Transcript: www.swsub.com

00:47.877 --> 00:50.545
Subtitles: Ju
www.top-series.net

01:14.588 --> 01:15.486
Episode 3x03

01:16.959 --> 01:18.114
I am so sorry.

01:18.376 --> 01:21.075
My apologies. I'm so busy today.
It's good to see all of you.

01:21.337 --> 01:23.369
That's quite all right.
Don't worry about it.

01:23.631 --> 01:25.337
Would now be a good time
to say few words

01:25.387 --> 01:27.307
about my wonderfully warm
and caring mother?

01:27.357 --> 01:30.528
- No. Just get to the reading part.
- Let's get on with it, man.

01:30.604 --> 01:31.711
Let's go.

01:32.830 --> 01:35.298
Which one of you is Frank Reynolds?

01:35.560 --> 01:36.567
Yo.

01:37.729 --> 01:40.511
I have something here that I need
to read to you from Barbara.

01:41.345 --> 01:43.080
"Frank, if your...

01:43.916 --> 01:47.727
"fat monkey heart is still beating,
then congratulations.

01:47.989 --> 01:52.471
"I want you to know that I hereby leave
all of your money to Bruce Mathis,

01:52.565 --> 01:54.108
"the real father of my children..."

01:54.370 --> 01:56.569
- What?
- Bruce Mathis?

01:56.831 --> 01:59.794
"... a handsome man
with a beautiful soul...

02:00.134 --> 02:02.283
"and a nicer penis."

02:02.545 --> 02:05.453
You're giving all my money
to that jerk-off?

02:05.715 --> 02:08.523
- I'm reading what's on the document.
- Why are you giving it to him?

02:08.619 --> 02:11.375
- She barely even knew him.
- I'm not giving any money to anybody.

02:11.727 --> 02:13.336
I'm just reading what's on a will.

02:13.598 --> 02:16.172
- Where is that rat bastard?
- Sir, I don't know...

02:16.434 --> 02:19.438
I wanna smash his face
until he's dead!

02:19.532 --> 02:20.619
Killed dead!

02:20.669 --> 02:23.679
Will you forget about Bruce!
Mom just gave away all of our money!

02:23.941 --> 02:26.759
You know what, we should
just move forward, okay?

02:27.418 --> 02:29.447
"For my darling son Dennis,"

02:29.560 --> 02:32.230
Presumably...
"I give you my house... "

02:32.492 --> 02:35.983
Yeah! Okay, now it's starting
to make sense. Read on.

02:36.245 --> 02:39.153
"... on the sole condition
that Frank not be allowed in. "

02:39.415 --> 02:40.821
- I'd never let him in.
- What?!

02:41.083 --> 02:42.084
"Deandra...

02:42.168 --> 02:44.158
"... you get nothing.

02:44.591 --> 02:46.997
"You were a disappointment
and a mistake."

02:47.047 --> 02:49.288
A mistake? We're twins.

02:50.101 --> 02:52.583
We were born at the same time.
You're not making any sense.

02:52.845 --> 02:54.418
Tell that bitch it doesn't make sense!

02:55.785 --> 02:59.314
I'm reading the words
that someone else wrote, okay?

03:00.416 --> 03:03.092
I don't know your mom,
never met your mom.

03:03.223 --> 03:07.456
In fact, I'm certainly not speaking
to your mom now, because she's dead.

03:07.860 --> 03:10.434
We know she's dead.
We're venting 'cause we're frustrated.

03:10.696 --> 03:12.979
You tell her she's a goddamn whore!

03:13.709 --> 03:15.064
Always been a whore!

03:15.326 --> 03:17.942
What about jewelry?
Does it say anything about jewelry?

03:18.204 --> 03:20.995
It does say something about
the jewelry in here in that,

03:21.045 --> 03:22.571
she wants to be buried in it.

03:22.833 --> 03:23.836
Goddamn it!

03:25.760 --> 03:27.635
She's taking it into the grave!

03:27.995 --> 03:30.871
Tell you what, you son of a bitch,
I'm very disappointed in you today.

03:31.133 --> 03:33.505
Very upset with you.
You tell her for me

03:33.643 --> 03:36.272
that I will be in touch
with her somehow.

03:36.357 --> 03:38.170
Tell her she's a bitch!

03:38.432 --> 03:40.381
These are awkward
situations often, and...

03:41.096 --> 03:43.294
I know it can be difficult...

03:44.101 --> 03:45.857
Thanks for the house, dude.

03:46.112 --> 03:49.890
You know... I didn't give you
the house. That's not how

03:50.152 --> 03:52.280
- this whole situation works.
- Yeah, you did!

03:54.534 --> 03:55.595
Jesus Christ.

04:01.108 --> 04:03.321
I got a plan to get back
at your mother.

04:03.583 --> 04:05.994
Too late...
I'm already full throttle over here.

04:06.044 --> 04:09.136
I'm gonna dig up her body
and snatch back that jewelry.

04:09.544 --> 04:10.786
That's insane!

04:11.370 --> 04:13.583
That woman is buried
down there like Mr. T.

04:13.668 --> 04:15.471
I gotta go while
the earth's still loose.

04:16.262 --> 04:18.377
I know how to get
the money back from Bruce.

04:19.483 --> 04:21.607
- What's your plan?
- All right.

04:23.673 --> 04:26.397
You call Brucey on the phone
and tell him that you want

04:26.472 --> 04:29.505
to introduce him to your new fiance.

04:30.547 --> 04:32.358
- Who's that?
- Me.

04:36.421 --> 04:38.356
This house sure brings back
a lot of memories.

04:38.618 --> 04:40.497
Look what I just found
in Dee's old room!

04:40.547 --> 04:43.544
It's her middle school diary, dude!
Ooh, yeah!

04:46.004 --> 04:47.156
Who gives a shit?

04:47.797 --> 04:50.857
This is her diary. It's got
all her secrets and shit in here.

04:51.006 --> 04:54.455
It says "Keep Out." There's a little
lock that we... We'll open it later.

04:54.717 --> 04:58.702
We are not reading Dee's
middle school diary to you, bro!

04:58.903 --> 05:00.669
We need to start the healing process.

05:02.266 --> 05:04.743
I'm devastated over here.
We need to throw a big-ass party.

05:04.865 --> 05:07.277
I need to be amongst my friends.
Let's call the crew.

05:07.400 --> 05:09.387
- Let's round the boys up!
- Round the crew up!

05:09.649 --> 05:11.055
Let's have a kick-ass party!

05:11.317 --> 05:14.141
- We got the diary! And the crew!
- The boys are back in town!

05:18.263 --> 05:20.635
I have two numbers in my phone:

05:21.264 --> 05:23.395
Charlie and Dennis.

05:25.427 --> 05:28.736
- Well, what about all our friends?
- What about Dooley? Call Dooley!

05:29.001 --> 05:31.283
- Dooley! He loves a good party!
- Let's call Dooley!

05:32.628 --> 05:34.078
Dooley in the house!

05:35.135 --> 05:36.581
Dooley killed himself.

05:39.929 --> 05:41.608
About two years back now.

05:42.640 --> 05:45.450
It's just a real sad, sad thing
for him and his family.

05:45.573 --> 05:46.590
I knew he was...

05:46.952 --> 05:49.071
- Depressed.
- Very sad...

05:49.670 --> 05:52.388
How about, uh, let's call Stash!
Let's get the Stash man!

05:53.558 --> 05:55.141
Stash? Stash man? What'd you do?

05:55.403 --> 05:57.045
- I set him on fire.
- Son of a bitch.

05:57.321 --> 05:59.869
Forget Stash. I didn't like him
anyway. Let's get Z-Man!

06:00.156 --> 06:01.480
I banged his sister.

06:03.035 --> 06:05.276
Sully! I got Sully's number.

06:05.538 --> 06:08.347
He has a restraing order against me.
Can't go within 500 feet of him.

06:08.582 --> 06:09.989
Plus, I banged his sister, too.

06:10.251 --> 06:11.888
- Did you really?
- She was gross.

06:11.953 --> 06:13.124
I remember that.

06:13.174 --> 06:14.785
So wait a minute, we got no friends?

06:15.202 --> 06:16.447
Looks like it, right?

06:18.830 --> 06:20.289
Wow, that hits home.

06:21.256 --> 06:22.385
That's terrible.

06:22.570 --> 06:25.425
Guys, guys, do you realize
what that means?

06:26.466 --> 06:28.635
If we were to all die suddenly,
just like my mom did,

06:28.776 --> 06:30.551
we'd have nobody left to mourn us.

06:32.857 --> 06:36.182
No one left to tell of our great
adventures and our glorious triumphs.

06:36.444 --> 06:40.102
- We got to make friends.
- All our triumphs and our tales and...

06:40.434 --> 06:42.354
We need to preserve our legacy.

06:42.616 --> 06:44.648
- That's what I'm saying.
- Our whole legacy!

06:44.910 --> 06:47.735
- Let's go out and make some friends.
- Let's do that. But first,

06:48.083 --> 06:50.690
who wants to run through
a quick chapter of this diary?

06:53.600 --> 06:56.076
- How's the ponytail look?
- It's ridiculous.

06:56.338 --> 06:59.121
Why are you wearing this whole get-up?
Bruce has never seen you.

06:59.383 --> 07:03.310
If we're gonna pull this thing off,
I got to turn into a liberal yahoo

07:03.413 --> 07:04.662
just like Bruce.

07:04.784 --> 07:07.630
When he gets here, I want you to hold
my hand through the whole thing.

07:08.886 --> 07:10.758
- I won't do that.
- Look,

07:11.020 --> 07:12.883
you've go to stop thinking of me
as your dad

07:13.013 --> 07:16.169
and start thinking of me
as your fiance, Seamus.

07:17.026 --> 07:18.807
Could we think of a less creepy angle?

07:19.069 --> 07:21.519
But this is a grift.
I mean, that's the way it is.

07:21.594 --> 07:23.187
You got to stay in character,

07:23.550 --> 07:24.563
all the time.

07:24.825 --> 07:27.358
As soon as you break character,
you blow the grift.

07:27.954 --> 07:29.763
- Hand. Hand.
- I don't want to touch you.

07:29.820 --> 07:31.483
- Holding hands.
- Goddamn it.

07:35.376 --> 07:37.409
Ah, my little girl, how you doing?
Are you okay?

07:37.671 --> 07:41.205
Well, no, no.
I'm very broken up inside.

07:43.175 --> 07:45.489
Bruce, this is Seamus,

07:46.022 --> 07:47.130
my fiance.

07:47.759 --> 07:49.964
I am also broken up.

07:51.412 --> 07:54.072
What say we all bring it on in
for a hug.

07:54.639 --> 07:55.778
We're doing hugs.

07:58.946 --> 08:01.124
Oh, I'm so sorry I missed
that funeral.

08:01.499 --> 08:04.823
We were in Uganda doing a lot
of work with the AIDS cris there...

08:05.115 --> 08:07.231
AIDS?
You touch anybody?

08:08.662 --> 08:09.817
Well, sure.

08:10.079 --> 08:12.203
What kind of shit is that?
You just hugged me!

08:12.306 --> 08:13.450
Why would you do that?

08:13.457 --> 08:14.456
Seamus is joking.

08:14.541 --> 08:16.699
He's got a... he's got
a very dry sense of humor.

08:16.961 --> 08:19.268
I'm not joking!
That shit is serious!

08:19.634 --> 08:21.407
I've got to take a shower now!

08:23.199 --> 08:27.052
- That's kind of... odd...
- Oh, yeah. Well, that's my guy.

08:27.174 --> 08:30.272
You know, he's got a little
bit of a germ problem.

08:30.488 --> 08:33.425
- I'll get him some books for that.
- He's... he's grieving and... yeah.

08:33.556 --> 08:36.594
- But you seem to be holding up okay.
- It's funny that I seem like that

08:36.856 --> 08:39.052
because I'm not holding up okay.
I'm very sad.

08:39.164 --> 08:41.588
- I'm devastated.
- Nothing tougher than losing a parent.

08:41.638 --> 08:42.683
Oh, it's the worst, and...

08:43.404 --> 08:46.137
So she gave you all of our money, huh?
All of... all of...

08:46.885 --> 08:48.960
All of our fortune...
she gave it to you.

08:49.514 --> 08:50.524
Weird, right?

08:51.592 --> 08:55.498
Good news is, it's all gonna go to help
the less fortunate, every penny.

08:55.663 --> 08:57.583
- That is good news.
- It's a done deal.

08:57.686 --> 08:58.949
Well, that's actually

08:59.211 --> 09:00.552
why we brought you here.

09:00.655 --> 09:02.831
Oh, see, Seamus and I have a plan.

09:03.287 --> 09:05.372
We want to adopt a ton of kids.

09:05.832 --> 09:06.913
Isn't that wonderful

09:07.177 --> 09:10.940
that we'll need to use our fortune,
that my mother gave you

09:11.400 --> 09:14.012
- to shove at these kids.
- You know what I think?

09:14.561 --> 09:16.528
I think I know exactly
what you and Seamus need.

09:16.621 --> 09:17.676
Can you sit tight?

09:18.041 --> 09:19.845
I'll get back to you
as soon as I can, okay?

09:20.623 --> 09:21.450
Okay.

09:27.447 --> 09:29.386
- Is he gone?
- Yeah, he's gone.

09:30.189 --> 09:31.815
Burn these clothes.

09:32.245 --> 09:34.618
Tracy, cancel all my appointments.

09:34.721 --> 09:37.025
It's time for my daughter
and that idiot who raised her

09:37.075 --> 09:38.197
to learn a lesson.

09:39.118 --> 09:41.167
Guys, I don't know
if I'm feeling this flyer idea.

09:41.317 --> 09:42.734
- Really?
- It's perfect, dude.

09:42.791 --> 09:45.317
How else are three guys in their
20s supposed to make friends?

09:45.373 --> 09:47.647
There's no system in place.
A flyer does all the work.

09:47.990 --> 09:50.375
All right, read back what we
got so far, 'cause I don't...

09:50.558 --> 09:51.563
"What up?

09:51.713 --> 09:53.639
"We're 3 cool guys looking
for other cool guys

09:53.789 --> 09:55.886
"who wanna hang out
in our party mansion."

09:56.534 --> 09:59.257
- Sounds a little gay, right?
- Yeah. It does sound gay.

09:59.408 --> 10:02.037
- Write: "Nothing sexual."
- Good. Okay.

10:02.188 --> 10:05.399
"Cool guys looking for other cool guys
who wanna hang out in out party mansion.

10:05.549 --> 10:07.455
"Nothing Sexual."

10:08.258 --> 10:09.798
And add "Fighters welcome", 'cause,

10:09.892 --> 10:11.535
tough dudes and some big dudes.

10:11.618 --> 10:13.868
I don't want a bunch of tough guys
wanting to fight me.

10:14.103 --> 10:15.828
It would be good
to have extra protection.

10:15.921 --> 10:19.822
- Extra protection and...
- Well, put "Fitness encouraged."

10:20.084 --> 10:21.617
- Beautiful.
- That sounds confusing.

10:21.845 --> 10:24.493
- I'll put "Dudes in good shape."
- There you go. That solves it.

10:24.755 --> 10:27.812
I like it. Okay, but we also
need a guy who's funny and fat.

10:27.906 --> 10:29.999
We need a funny fat guy.
'Cause every crew has one.

10:30.261 --> 10:32.659
Well, I'm the funny fat guy,
so don't worry about that.

10:32.725 --> 10:34.687
- You're not fat, dude.
- You're also not funny.

10:34.884 --> 10:36.880
I want somebody who does
observational humor...

10:37.142 --> 10:39.717
That would be good.
Observational humor is cool.

10:39.802 --> 10:41.552
I'm just gonna put
"Nothing sexual" again

10:41.814 --> 10:43.457
- just to reiterate.
- Underline it.

10:43.616 --> 10:45.180
Please. Be very clear with that.

10:45.525 --> 10:48.332
And I'm thinking that the flyer
should be in the shape of a beermug.

10:49.008 --> 10:51.722
- Too complicated.
- Yeah. What about, uh, bicep?

10:51.938 --> 10:53.750
A bicep. Bicep's good.

10:53.852 --> 10:56.180
- All right, let's go with the bicep.
- Okay, read.

10:56.349 --> 10:57.692
Here we go. "What up?"

10:57.955 --> 11:00.006
"We're three cool guys
looking for other cool guys

11:00.072 --> 11:02.962
"who want to hang out in our party
mansion. Nothing sexual.

11:03.012 --> 11:04.526
"Dudes in good shape encouraged.

11:04.576 --> 11:08.294
"If you're fat, you should be able
to find humor in the little things.

11:08.482 --> 11:10.782
Again, "nothing sexual". Underlined.

11:10.949 --> 11:12.285
- Okay.
- Great.

11:12.637 --> 11:15.575
- I have no problem with that.
- No. Let's go meet some men.

11:21.382 --> 11:24.518
Lookin' good, bro.
Looking very good.

11:24.922 --> 11:25.929
I'm sorry?

11:26.274 --> 11:27.889
Oh, your pants... nice cut.

11:28.015 --> 11:30.639
That vertical line on the side
gives your body good length.

11:32.332 --> 11:33.843
Do you work here?

11:34.908 --> 11:36.684
I'm just looking to meet some new guys.

11:36.768 --> 11:38.919
I saw you from across the way
and I thought, yeah,

11:39.078 --> 11:41.774
this guy's got a good sense of style.
He's about the same age.

11:41.897 --> 11:44.950
Got a nice crop of blond hair. We could
definitely use a blond in the crew.

11:45.038 --> 11:47.159
Mix things up a little bit.
Why don't you just...

11:48.033 --> 11:49.828
take a look at that flyer there?

11:50.671 --> 11:51.864
Is this a penis?

11:52.117 --> 11:53.832
A penis... No, it's a...

11:54.440 --> 11:55.584
It's a bicep.

11:58.467 --> 12:00.881
Oh, right. Party Mansion.

12:01.143 --> 12:02.257
- Exactly.
- Cool.

12:02.807 --> 12:03.967
I'll swing by.

12:04.351 --> 12:05.816
- You'll swing by?
- Yeah, sure.

12:05.900 --> 12:08.085
Just come by the address.
We'll be there partying.

12:08.198 --> 12:11.308
- Yeah, at the Party Mansion.
- Yeah, you're gonna be perfect, man.

12:11.570 --> 12:12.726
See you there.

12:12.988 --> 12:15.125
Oh, I should give him
some more for his friends.

12:17.763 --> 12:19.250
Oh, son of a bitch.

12:19.912 --> 12:21.382
Penis? No, it's a bicep.

12:21.504 --> 12:26.060
Bro, I just had the most perfect
blond guy slip right through my fingers.

12:26.182 --> 12:29.340
I mean, I had him in the palm of my hand
and then... he was gone,

12:29.390 --> 12:32.162
you know what I mean? This guy would
have been perfect for you.

12:32.940 --> 12:35.231
What's up with this beefcake?
Is he coming to the party?

12:35.288 --> 12:36.649
- Big time.
- Great.

12:36.734 --> 12:39.012
- He didn't read the flyer.
- I read the flyer.

12:39.181 --> 12:41.588
- He didn't understand it.
- I understood it... perfectly.

12:43.967 --> 12:46.108
Okay, we need to take a
second look at this flyer.

12:46.174 --> 12:47.812
- Uh, yeah, dude.
- Guys,

12:48.148 --> 12:51.295
check out who I just met buying
a crossbow. This dude is the shit.

12:51.464 --> 12:54.877
I shall use this crossbow to
pierce my broken heart.

12:54.989 --> 12:55.994
Yeah.

12:56.792 --> 12:58.435
All... right, dude.

13:01.578 --> 13:03.777
Dude, is that guy awesome or what?
He's like a poet.

13:04.203 --> 13:05.362
That guy's not awesome.

13:05.856 --> 13:09.951
Dude, do you know how hard it is to find
a passionate guy like that these days?

13:10.017 --> 13:11.144
They don't make 'em anymore.

13:11.205 --> 13:14.059
You should see how passionate he got
when I showed him the dick flyer.

13:14.134 --> 13:15.539
You knew that it was a dick?

13:15.801 --> 13:18.333
Yeah, I thought we changed it.
I thought you were changing it.

13:18.595 --> 13:20.326
It was always meant to be a bicep.

13:20.380 --> 13:23.522
Then why did you cut it like...
'cause it looks totally like a dick.

13:23.616 --> 13:26.383
I thought, let's go with the dick thing.
It's more masculine anyway.

13:27.118 --> 13:29.887
I mean, shit, if you wanted it
to be a bicep, it needs more veins.

13:31.752 --> 13:33.151
I can't wear this.

13:33.574 --> 13:35.263
I got to go home get another costume.

13:35.529 --> 13:37.254
There's no time.
Just sit down and shut up

13:37.329 --> 13:39.078
and wait for Bruce
to get back the money.

13:39.798 --> 13:40.804
All right.

13:40.926 --> 13:43.574
But I can't promise
that I'm not going to go berserk

13:43.686 --> 13:45.489
if he tries to give me AIDS again.

13:46.059 --> 13:47.721
He wasn't trying to give you AIDS.

13:47.796 --> 13:51.533
Jesus Christ, you're the one who's going
on and on about staying in character.

13:51.795 --> 13:54.203
- Yeah, you're right.
- Look, we can do this, okay?

13:54.465 --> 13:57.774
We've to go along with whatever
he throws at us. So close to that money.

13:58.241 --> 13:59.246
